      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The borough’s name comes from George L. Ziegler, who founded the town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delta%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Slate quarrying began in 1734, making Delta part of the Peach Bottom Slate Region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.witnessingyork.com/mapping-meaning/delta-its-region-slate-roofs-slate-foundations/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Maryland Central Railroad reached Delta in 1883, turning it into a key stop between Baltimore and York.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delta%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Welsh miners shaped the town’s slate industry, and their work still appears on historic roofs today.",
